.TH sasl_oauthbearer 5 "August 2026" "crudeoauth" "File Formats and Conventions"
.SH NAME
OAUTHBEARER \- SASL mechanism for OAuth 2.0 bearer token authentication
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/ldap/sasl2/slapd.conf
.br
SASL configuration file for OpenLDAP or another Cyrus SASL consumer.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B OAUTHBEARER
SASL mechanism implements OAuth 2.0 bearer token authentication according to RFC 7628.
The server side validates signed JWT access tokens against locally configured trusted JWKS files and applies issuer, audience, time, scope, authorized-party, algorithm, and username policy checks.
.PP
The JWT signature is verified using the key selected by the token's
.B kid
header. JWKS entries that are not usable for signature verification, for example encryption keys, are ignored. A JWK
.B alg
value, when present, must be compatible with the JWT algorithm.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration options are specified in the SASL configuration file, commonly
.I /etc/ldap/sasl2/slapd.conf
for OpenLDAP.
.PP
Options whose names end in a number can be repeated by using consecutive indices starting at 0.
.TP
.B mech_list
Must include
.BR OAUTHBEARER .
.TP
.B oauthbearer_grace
Allowed clock skew in seconds when checking
.BR nbf ,
.B iat
and
.B exp .
The default is 3 seconds. The grace period does not extend the configured lifetime of a token; it only tolerates clock skew around token timestamps.
.TP
.B oauthbearer_userid
JWT claim used as the SASL authentication identity (authcid).
The default is
.BR preferred_username .
.TP
.B oauthbearer_disallowed_username0
Reject the resolved username if it matches this value. The comparison is case-insensitive.
This option can be repeated as
.BR oauthbearer_disallowed_username1 ,
.B oauthbearer_disallowed_username2
and so on. It can be used, for example, to prevent an identity provider from authenticating directly as privileged local accounts such as
.BR root .
.TP
.B oauthbearer_trusted_jwks0
Path to a JWKS file containing trusted verification keys. At least one JWKS file must be configured.
Multiple files may be specified using consecutive numeric suffixes.
.TP
.B oauthbearer_trusted_iss0
Trusted value of the
.B iss
(Issuer) claim. Tokens from other issuers are rejected.
.TP
.B oauthbearer_trusted_aud0
Trusted value of the
.B aud
(Audience) claim. At least one trusted audience must be configured. A token is accepted if its audience matches a configured value.
.TP
.B oauthbearer_trusted_azp0
Trusted value of the optional
.B azp
(Authorized Party) claim. If trusted authorized parties are configured, a present
.B azp
claim must match one of them.
.TP
.B oauthbearer_required_scope0
Require the named OAuth scope. Multiple scopes may be required by using consecutive numeric suffixes. The token's
.B scope
claim is interpreted as a space-separated OAuth scope list.
.TP
.B oauthbearer_allowed_alg0
Optional allow-list for JWT signature algorithms. If omitted, the built-in algorithm policy is used.
If one or more values are configured, only those algorithms are accepted, subject also to the disallow-list and JWK compatibility checks.
Supported names are
.BR RS256 ,
.BR RS384 ,
.BR RS512 ,
.BR PS256 ,
.BR PS384 ,
.BR PS512 ,
.BR ES256 ,
.BR ES384
and
.BR EdDSA .
.TP
.B oauthbearer_disallowed_alg0
Optional deny-list for JWT signature algorithms. A disallowed algorithm is rejected even if it is part of the built-in policy or explicitly allowed with
.BR oauthbearer_allowed_algN .
This is useful for disabling an algorithm locally without having to reproduce the complete allow-list.
.TP
.B oauthbearer_no_tls
Set to
.B 1
to disable the plugin's TLS requirement.
The default is to require an encrypted connection. Disabling this check is not recommended because bearer tokens can be replayed by anyone who obtains them.
.SH JWT VALIDATION
The server verifies the JWT signature before accepting the token claims.
It requires a known
.B kid
and selects the corresponding key only from the configured JWKS data.
Token-provided key URLs or embedded keys are not used as trust sources.
.PP
The configured issuer and audience are checked. If configured, authorized party and required scopes are also checked.
The
.BR nbf ,
.B iat
and
.B exp
claims are checked when present using
.B oauthbearer_grace
for clock skew.
The configured username claim must be present and must not match a configured disallowed username.
.PP
.B RSA-OAEP
is a JWE key-management algorithm, not a JWT signature algorithm. JWKS files may contain such encryption keys; they are ignored for JWS signature verification rather than causing the complete JWKS to be rejected.
.SH MAPPING TO LDAP DN
After a successful SASL bind, OpenLDAP provides a SASL identity such as:
.IP
uid=username,cn=oauthbearer,cn=auth
.PP
It can be mapped to a directory DN with
.B authz-regexp
in
.I slapd.conf
for example:
.PP
.nf
authz-regexp
    uid=([^,]*),cn=oauthbearer,cn=auth
    ldap:///dc=example,dc=org??sub?uid=$1
.fi
